F. What singles out j = 2 (N = 36)?
================================================================================================
  (Ljunggren 1946) j <= 3000 with m_j triangular, i.e. N_j = (triangular)^2 = sum of cubes: [0, 1, 2]  -> m = [0, 1, 6], N = [0, 1, 36]
  j <= 3000 with N_j 3-smooth: [1, 2]  -> N = [1, 36]
  n_2 = 8 = 8*m_1^2, n_2 + 1 = 9 = u_1^2 : the pair (8, 9) IS the fundamental solution 3^2 - 8*1^2 = 1

