H. Mirror / control for the identity  n_(j+1) + n_(j-1) = 2 (3 n_j + 1)
   For any odd q the unit q + sqrt(q^2-1) has trace 2q, so with u = (q-1) n + 1 (centre -1/(q-1),
   where n -> q n + 1 is u -> q u) the same identity holds with q n + 1.  q = 3 is not singled out.
================================================================================================
   q=3: u^2 - 8 y^2 = 1, unit 3+sqrt(8);  n = (u-1)/2 integral for all j: True;  n_j = [0, 1, 8, 49, 288, 1681];  n_(j+1)+n_(j-1) = 2(3n_j+1): True
   q=5: u^2 - 24 y^2 = 1, unit 5+sqrt(24);  n = (u-1)/4 integral for all j: True;  n_j = [0, 1, 12, 121, 1200, 11881];  n_(j+1)+n_(j-1) = 2(5n_j+1): True
   q=7: u^2 - 48 y^2 = 1, unit 7+sqrt(48);  n = (u-1)/6 integral for all j: True;  n_j = [0, 1, 16, 225, 3136, 43681];  n_(j+1)+n_(j-1) = 2(7n_j+1): True
   q=9: u^2 - 80 y^2 = 1, unit 9+sqrt(80);  n = (u-1)/8 integral for all j: True;  n_j = [0, 1, 20, 361, 6480, 116281];  n_(j+1)+n_(j-1) = 2(9n_j+1): True
   mirror (3x-1): with n' = n + 1 (so N = T_(n'-1)) the identity reads n'_(j+1) + n'_(j-1) = 2(3n'_j - 1): True

